    "turn_text": "Hugh is probably a better radio talk show hosting as a reporter in that regard because neither Donald nor I never talked to each other about me being the vice president. I think he picked a very good man in Mike Pence. I've gotten to know Donald over the last 18 months or so from the time he started a campaign. He was in Arkansas as our Republican annual fundraising dinner keynoter. Just a few weeks after he started the campaign in 2015, I wasn't there. I was actually traveling in Europe. That's when I was in Vienna at the International Atomic Agency, where I discovered the secret side deals, which so much not have been made, but he got a chance to meet my parents, and he always asked about my parents and their health. We had conversations throughout the course of the campaign, especially about defense policy, the defense budget. I was pleased to see in his speech a few months ago, he called for substantial increases in defense spending. in our conversations, whether they're one-on-one or with larger groups of senators. He's always struck me as someone who's serious about the task in front of him and eager to make America great again. That's why he campaigned on that slogan.",
