    "turn_text": "expand it beyond a legislative perspective, although that's certainly important. But there's a lot of other things in that first 100 days that needs to happen. We all campaigned throughout 2016 on the Supreme Court. And Donald Trump has published a list of a couple dozen potential nominees to the Supreme Court. I hope that he makes a decision and announces that decision sooner rather than later. So the Senate can begin hearings on January 3rd and hopefully have a vote by the end of January. That's vitally important. Second, for the last six years, Barack Obama has implemented much of his agenda through executive action. Donald Trump campaigned on rolling back a lot of those executive orders. For example, his efforts in 2014 to grant de facto legal status to up to 5 million illegal immigrants. Donald Trump promised to roll this back. I hope he does in short order as soon as he takes office. He should not go further and try to implement a Republican policy agenda. through executive action, the way Barack Obama did, a Democratic agenda, he should simply roll back Barack Obama's executive orders. And then third, from a legislative standpoint, there's the urgent, which are things like a defense supplemental bill to stop some of the troop drawdowns and to make sure that all the troops are getting the kind of training they need before the overseas. And then there's the longer term and more consequential, like a fundamental rewriting of our nation's immigration laws. Some of those, like the defense supplemental bill, could happen in the first hundred days. A rewrite of our immigration laws might take several months.",
