    "turn_text": "leave that to Donald Trump to make those decisions. There's many qualified Americans. I will say that there's one person who we should get back into the government, and that's retired Marine General John Kelly. John Kelly served for 46 years in active duty. He concluded his career by being the combatant commander for Southern Command, so all of Latin America. which is the least militarized command, you might say, and therefore the most diplomatic one. John Kelly is a deeply experienced warrior who used to ride along with Marines and Iraq specifically to be with him in action, but he's also a highly skilled diplomat, too. And I would encourage the president elect to find a position in his administration for John Kelly. I would have said the same thing to Hillary Clinton or to anyone else that ran for president last year. John Kelly is is too talented and skilled an American who loves his country too much not to have him at a key position in any administration?",
