    "turn_idx": 45,
    "turn_text": "Let me ask you a kind of a political question. Some people have said Kelly Aiot is being considered for Secretary of Defense. She wasn't quite a never-trumper. But more generally, obviously there was a split, somewhat of a split within the party between those who got behind Trump and then a contingent of kind of figures in Washington and New York who didn't get behind Trump. Some of them have talents that have been used in administrations before. Do you think that the Trump administration should seek to try to mend those heels and bring some of those people into the administration, or do you think they shouldn't, since they didn't support Trump, should not be in the administration?",
