    "turn_text": "to turn your life around from such a bad decision. I would say that I would encourage anyone who ask me about running for office to do so. Our country needs good men and women running for office, whether it's for president or whether it's for school board and city council. I would also advise them though that there are too many twists and turns in life and politics to set your eyes on one single position or one single office that you should simply try to find places where you can serve your fellow man and to give back to a country that has given us so much. There are obvious things that you can do to position yourself for that, like, you know, go work on a campaign or volunteer for a local party or be a part of a local party committee. So I encourage that activity and I encourage people to run for office. But but ultimately it's, you know, very hard to plot down exactly where you think you're going to be in life. And, you know, I certainly wouldn't have guessed, you know, 10 years ago when I was in Iraq as a platoon leader that I was going to be in the United States Senate right now.",
